course: dictionary
lesson: 8906
title: Shutter, one word with several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. To work out which one you need, read the words around it. The context tells you what kind of shutter is meant.
explain: «Sockets have little shutters inside the holes» tells you the shutters are small parts, not a window cover. «A UK plug has three pins» and «the earth pin opens little shutters in the socket» show the shutters open only when a plug goes in.
explain: «A lyrebird copies a camera shutter» has camera in it, so the shutter is the part of a camera that lets light in. Always test your meaning: put it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A shutter is a wooden or metal cover on a window. You open and close it to keep out light, wind or burglars.
fact: In a camera, the shutter is a tiny part that opens for a moment to let light in when you take a photo.
fact: In a socket, the shutters cover the holes until a plug's pin opens them.
fact: To shutter a shop means to close it, often for good. A shop shutter is a metal roll-down cover on a shop front.
exercise: «A socket is the end of wires from the fuse box, and its shutters cover the holes until a plug's earth pin opens them.» What do the shutters do? | They let the wind into the room | They make the socket light up | *They cover the holes until a plug opens them | They hold the wires in place
exercise: In a camera, what is the shutter? | The ring that holds the lens | The flash that lights up a dark room | The wooden cover on a window | *The tiny part that opens for a moment to let light in
exercise: To shutter a shop means to | *close it, often for good | paint its front door | open it very early | make it bigger
test: «Mains electricity is strong enough to kill, so homes are full of guards: shutters inside sockets, fuses that melt, and switches in the fuse box that cut the power in a blink.» What are the shutters in this sentence? | Blinds that make a room darker for sleeping | *Guards that keep people safe from electricity | Doors for cupboards in the kitchen | Windows that let in fresh air
test: Which one is a shop shutter? | A wooden frame that holds glass in a window | A tiny part inside a camera | A three-pin plug with a fuse inside | *A metal roll-down cover on a shop front
exam: Which meaning fits «A lyrebird copies a camera shutter and a chainsaw.»? | *The tiny part of a camera that opens to let in light | A wooden cover on a window | To close a shop for good | A metal roll-down cover on a shop front
